The [[2021 Copa América]] was an international [[Association football|football]] tournament held in [[Brazil]] from 13 June to 10 July 2021. The ten national teams involved in the tournament were required to register a squad of up to 28 players, including at least three goalkeepers, an increase over the usual number of 23 players allowed. Only players in these squads were eligible to take part in the tournament.<ref name="regulations">{{cite web|url=https://www.conmebol.com/sites/default/files/reglamento-copa-america-2021.pdf|title=REGLAMENTO CONMEBOL COPA AMÉRICA 2021|publisher=[[CONMEBOL]]|date=12 May 2021|language=es|access-date=3 June 2021|archive-date=14 May 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210514204502/https://www.conmebol.com/sites/default/files/reglamento-copa-america-2021.pdf|url-status=dead}}</ref>

On 22 March 2021, during a virtual meeting of its Council, [[CONMEBOL]] confirmed adjustments in the tournament regulations, several of these related to the player rosters, taking into account the conditions imposed by the [[COVID-19 pandemic in South America|COVID-19 pandemic]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.conmebol.com/es/consejo-evaluo-el-exito-de-la-conmebol-libertadores-femenina-y-los-avances-de-la-conmebol-copa|title=Consejo evaluó el éxito de la CONMEBOL Libertadores Femenina y los avances de la CONMEBOL Copa América|publisher=CONMEBOL|date=22 March 2021|language=es}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.ole.com.ar/seleccion/seleccion-copaamerica-cambios-covid_0_LLDXEOsqC.html|title=Los cambios inéditos por Covid en la Copa América|publisher=[[Olé (sports newspaper)|Olé]]|last=Maffei|first=Sergio|date=28 April 2021|language=es}}</ref>

Initially the ten national teams were required to register a provisional list with up to fifty players and then a final list of 23 players. However, on 28 May 2021, CONMEBOL decided to increase the provisional list up to sixty players and the final list up to 28 players at the request of some national associations.<ref name="increase of players">{{cite web|url=https://www.conmebol.com/es/aumento-en-lista-final-de-jugadores-y-lista-provisoria-para-la-conmebol-copa-america-2021|title=Aumento en Lista Final de jugadores y Lista Provisoria para la CONMEBOL Copa América 2021|publisher=CONMEBOL|date=28 May 2021|language=es}}</ref> Each national team had to submit its provisional list of up to fifty players to CONMEBOL by 27 April 2021, 18:00 [[Time in Paraguay|PYT]] ([[UTC−04:00|UTC−4]]) (Regulations Article 25) and could also register up to ten additional players until 1 June. Taking into consideration the fact that matchdays 7 and 8 of [[2022 FIFA World Cup qualification (CONMEBOL)|CONMEBOL's FIFA World Cup qualifiers]] were played only a few days before the start of the tournament, the final list of up to 28 players per national team could be submitted to CONMEBOL by 10 June 2021, 12:00 [[Time in Paraguay|PYT]] ([[UTC−04:00|UTC−4]]), three days prior to the opening match of the tournament. All players in the final selection must not have been excluded from the provisional list (Regulations Article 27).

Despite the increase of players in the final lists, teams could still only name a maximum of 23 players on the match list for each tournament fixture (of which twelve were substitutes).<ref name="increase of players"/>

Once the final lists were registered, teams were only permitted to make replacements in cases of serious injuries up to 24 hours before their first match. Teams were also permitted to replace an injured goalkeeper with another at any time during the tournament (Regulations Article 28). In addition, any player with positive [[Polymerase chain reaction|PCR]] tests for [[SARS-CoV-2]] could be replaced before and during the tournament (Regulations Article 30).<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.conmebol.com/es/consejo-de-conmebol-modifica-reglamento-art-301-de-la-copa-america-2021|title=Consejo de CONMEBOL modifica reglamento – Art. 30.1 de la Copa América 2021|publisher=CONMEBOL|date=11 June 2021|language=es}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.conmebol.com/sites/default/files/circular_ndeg18_-_ca2021_-_modificacion_art._30.1_-_sustitucion_de_jugadores_por_covid-19.pdf|title=CIRCULAR N° 18|publisher=CONMEBOL|date=11 June 2021|language=es}}</ref> All substitutes had to have the approval of the CONMEBOL Medical Commission and the replacement players did not need to be in the provisional list.

Before starting the [[2021 Copa América knockout stage|final stage]] of the tournament, teams were able to replace a total of three players from their final list,<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.conmebol.com/es/calendario-de-la-conmebol-copa-america-2021|title=Calendario de la CONMEBOL Copa América 2021|publisher=CONMEBOL|date=13 August 2021|language=es}}</ref> with the replacement players coming from the provisional list (Regulations Article 29).

The final lists were published by CONMEBOL on 10 June 2021.<ref>{{cite news|url=https://copaamerica.com/en/news/squad-lists-CONMEBOL-copa-america-2021/|title=Squad lists for all countries at the CONMEBOL Copa America 2021|publisher=CONMEBOL|website=copaamerica.com|date=10 June 2021|access-date=14 June 2021|archive-date=23 June 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210623211813/https://copaamerica.com/en/news/squad-lists-conmebol-copa-america-2021/|url-status=dead}}</ref>

The age listed for each player is as of 13 June 2021, the first day of the tournament. The numbers of caps and goals listed for each player do not include any matches played after the start of the tournament. A flag is included for coaches who are of a different nationality than their own national team.

