===Venezuela===
Head coach: {{flagicon|POR}} [[José Peseiro]]

[[Venezuela national football team|Venezuela]]'s 49-man provisional list was announced on 12 and 13 May 2021.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.federacionvenezolanadefutbol.org/la-vinotinto-definio-su-lista-preliminar-para-la-conmebol-copa-america-2021/|title=La Vinotinto definió su Lista Preliminar para la CONMEBOL Copa América 2021|publisher=[[Venezuelan Football Federation]]|date=12 May 2021|language=es}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.federacionvenezolanadefutbol.org/cuerpo-tecnico-de-la-vinotinto-amplio-lista-preliminar-para-copa-america-con-jugadores-de-la-liga-futve/|title=Cuerpo Técnico de La Vinotinto amplió Lista Preliminar para Copa América con jugadores de la Liga Futve|publisher=Venezuelan Football Federation|date=13 May 2021|language=es}}</ref> The final squad of 28 players was announced on 10 June 2021.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.federacionvenezolanadefutbol.org/la-vinotinto-tiene-sus-28-guerreros-para-la-conmebol-copa-america-2021/|title=La Vinotinto tiene sus 28 guerreros para la CONMEBOL Copa América 2021|publisher=Venezuelan Football Federation|date=10 June 2021|language=es}}</ref> On 12 June 2021, CONMEBOL and the [[Venezuelan Football Federation]] reported that eleven members of its delegation, eight of them footballers, had tested positive for SARS-CoV-2.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.conmebol.com/es/comunicado-conmebol-4|title=Comunicado CONMEBOL|publisher=CONMEBOL|date=12 June 2021|language=es}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.conmebol.com/sites/default/files/cmua.055-2021_casos_positivos_venezuela_11_junio_ca_bra_2021__0.pdf|title=CMUA.055-2021|publisher=CONMEBOL|date=12 June 2021|access-date=12 June 2021|language=es|archive-date=13 June 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210613110851/https://www.conmebol.com/sites/default/files/cmua.055-2021_casos_positivos_venezuela_11_junio_ca_bra_2021__0.pdf|url-status=dead}}</ref> Consequently, fifteen additional players were called up to join the squad.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.federacionvenezolanadefutbol.org/comunicado-120621/|title=COMUNICADO|publisher=Venezuelan Football Federation|date=12 June 2021|access-date=12 June 2021|language=es}}</ref> Midfielder and captain [[Tomás Rincón]] and goalkeeper [[Rafael Romo]] tested positive for SARS-CoV-2 and were replaced by [[Francisco La Mantía]] and [[Luis Romero (Venezuelan footballer)|Luis Romero]] respectively on 12 June.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://primicia.com.ve/deportes/otra-baja-de-venezuela-para-la-copa-america-tomas-rincon-positivo-por-covid-19/|title=Otra baja de Venezuela para la Copa América: Tomás Rincón positivo por COVID-19|publisher=Primicia|first=Fabiana|last=Dos Reis|date=12 June 2021|access-date=12 June 2021|language=es }}</ref> After the team's first match, defender [[Jhon Chancellor]] and midfielder [[Jhon Murillo]] tested positive for SARS-CoV-2 and were replaced by [[José Manuel Velázquez]] and [[Jan Carlos Hurtado]] respectively.<ref>{{Cite web | url=https://juanfutbol.com/articulo/cperez/venezuela-anuncia-nuevos-casos-de-covid19-en-su-plantilla | title=Venezuela anuncia nuevos casos de Covid-19 en su plantilla }}</ref>

